abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of VAST, the propagation-aware active semi-supervised
  learning framework presented in "Which Cases Are Worth Labeling for Microservice
  Root Cause Localization?" VAST combines the Symptom-Conditioned Ordered
  Propagation Encoder (SCOPE), PropCover acquisition, and Root-Set-Conditioned
  Completion (RSC) to learn candidate root-cause rankings for services, instances,
  or hosts from metrics, logs, traces, and typed topology in labeled and permitted
  unlabeled cases. PropCover selects complete cases for annotation based on
  additional propagation coverage. Training combines root supervision, observation
  self-supervision, and source-conditioned learning without treating inferred root
  hypotheses as verified labels. Datasets, frozen split assets, trained weights,
  completed benchmark results, and the complete paper-experiment automation suite
  are not included.
keywords:
  - microservices
  - root cause localization
  - multimodal active learning
  - semi-supervised learning
  - propagation coverage
  - candidate root-cause ranking
